IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fcfca-dates`
IMPORT `fcfca-claims`

-- Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021 (Cth) -- worked cases for the questions of the party bringing
-- (or answering) a civil claim in the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2).
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- Sourced from the Federal Register of Legislation, Commonwealth of Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

`family law` MEANS `a family law proceeding (under the Family Law Act 1975, the Marriage Act 1961 or a Territory family law; s 132(1)(a)-(c))`
`child support` MEANS `a child support proceeding (under the Child Support (Assessment) Act 1989 or the Child Support (Registration and Collection) Act 1988; s 132(1)(d))`
`general` MEANS `another civil proceeding (general federal law, Fair Work, discrimination, a Commonwealth tenancy dispute or other)`

-- A test helper: whether an optional list of answers holds a given line.
GIVEN line IS A STRING, answers IS A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the answer includes` line answers MEANS
    CONSIDER answers
    WHEN JUST xs THEN elem line xs
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

§ `s 7 -- the kinds of proceeding`

#ASSERT `s 7 -- a family law or child support proceeding` `family law`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- a family law or child support proceeding` `child support`
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 7 -- a family law or child support proceeding` `general`))
#ASSERT `a proceeding under the Family Law Act 1975` `family law`
-- A child support proceeding is a "family law or child support proceeding" but not one "under the Family Law Act 1975".
#ASSERT (NOT (`a proceeding under the Family Law Act 1975` `child support`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`a proceeding under the Family Law Act 1975` `general`))

§ `s 135 -- which Division`

-- A Fair Work Act underpayment claim (FW Act s 567 sends it to the Fair Work Division).
#ASSERT `s 135 -- which Division my claim goes to` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Fair Work Division (s 135(3))`
-- A debt claim under general federal law.
#ASSERT `s 135 -- which Division my claim goes to` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the General Division (s 135(4))`
-- Required in both: the Chief Judge's direction.
#ASSERT `s 135 -- which Division my claim goes to` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Division the Chief Judge directs; until a direction, the Act does not say (s 135(5))`
-- Required only in the General Division by another Act: the General Division.
#ASSERT `s 135 -- which Division my claim goes to` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the General Division (s 135(4))`

§ `ss 136, 137, 185 -- how my claim is heard`

#ASSERT `ss 136, 137, 185 -- how my claim is heard` `general` FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST "by a single Judge (s 137(1))", "without a jury (s 185)", "in open court, which includes a hearing made public by video link, audio link or other means (s 136(2), (2A))"
#ASSERT elem "in court with the public, or the persons named, excluded by order (s 136(7))" (`ss 136, 137, 185 -- how my claim is heard` `general` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT elem "by a Judge sitting in Chambers (s 136(3), (4))" (`ss 136, 137, 185 -- how my claim is heard` `general` FALSE TRUE)
-- Exclusion and Chambers both: the exclusion order is answered first.
#ASSERT elem "in court with the public, or the persons named, excluded by order (s 136(7))" (`ss 136, 137, 185 -- how my claim is heard` `general` TRUE TRUE)
-- Family law: s 136 does not apply; still a single Judge and no jury.
#ASSERT elem "open court or not: s 136 does not apply; the Family Law Act 1975 s 97 governs (s 136(1))" (`ss 136, 137, 185 -- how my claim is heard` `family law` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT elem "without a jury (s 185)" (`ss 136, 137, 185 -- how my claim is heard` `child support` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT count (`ss 136, 137, 185 -- how my claim is heard` `general` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 3

§ `s 133 -- Commonwealth tenancy disputes`

`direct C` MEANS `the Commonwealth is my lessor, licensor or grantor directly (not a sublessor or sublicensor)`
`not direct C` MEANS `the Commonwealth is a sublessor or sublicensor, or not my landlord at all`
`direct me` MEANS `I am the lessee, licensee or grantee directly (not a sublessee or sublicensee)`
`sub me` MEANS `I am a sublessee or sublicensee`

-- A tenant of a Commonwealth-owned house in arrears dispute.
#ASSERT `s 133 -- can I bring my Commonwealth tenancy dispute in Division 2` `direct C` `direct me` FALSE TRUE TRUE `rent or other payments under the arrangement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 133 -- can I bring my Commonwealth tenancy dispute in Division 2` `direct C` `direct me` FALSE TRUE TRUE `ending the arrangement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 133 -- can I bring my Commonwealth tenancy dispute in Division 2` `direct C` `direct me` FALSE FALSE TRUE `possession, occupation or use of the land` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A permission (not a lease or licence) over Commonwealth land; and over land the Commonwealth does not own.
#ASSERT `s 133 -- can I bring my Commonwealth tenancy dispute in Division 2` `direct C` `direct me` FALSE TRUE FALSE `possession, occupation or use of the land` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 133 -- can I bring my Commonwealth tenancy dispute in Division 2` `direct C` `direct me` FALSE FALSE FALSE `possession, occupation or use of the land` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A Commonwealth employee as tenant; a subtenant; the Commonwealth as sublessor; a dispute about something else.
#ASSERT `s 133 -- can I bring my Commonwealth tenancy dispute in Division 2` `direct C` `direct me` TRUE TRUE TRUE `rent or other payments under the arrangement` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 133 -- can I bring my Commonwealth tenancy dispute in Division 2` `direct C` `sub me` FALSE TRUE TRUE `rent or other payments under the arrangement` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 133 -- can I bring my Commonwealth tenancy dispute in Division 2` `not direct C` `direct me` FALSE TRUE TRUE `rent or other payments under the arrangement` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 133 -- can I bring my Commonwealth tenancy dispute in Division 2` `direct C` `direct me` FALSE TRUE TRUE `something else` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 143 -- summary judgment`

#ASSERT `s 143 -- summary judgment` `general` `I am bringing the claim` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Court may give judgment for me now, on the whole or that part (s 143)`
#ASSERT `s 143 -- summary judgment` `general` `I am defending the claim` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Court may give judgment for me now, on the whole or that part (s 143)`
#ASSERT `s 143 -- summary judgment` `general` `I am bringing the claim` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the Court may give judgment against me now, on the whole or that part (s 143)`
#ASSERT `s 143 -- summary judgment` `general` `I am bringing the claim` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 143 does not reach it on these facts; the case goes on`
#ASSERT `s 143 -- summary judgment` `family law` `I am bringing the claim` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 143 does not apply: Family Law Act jurisdiction (s 143(5); see Family Law Act s 102QAB)`
-- Child support is not "jurisdiction under the Family Law Act 1975": s 143 applies.
#ASSERT `s 143 -- summary judgment` `child support` `I am defending the claim` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the Court may give judgment against me now, on the whole or that part (s 143)`

§ `s 176 -- discovery and interrogatories`

#ASSERT `s 176 -- can I have discovery or interrogatories` `family law` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 176 -- can I have discovery or interrogatories` `child support` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 176 -- can I have discovery or interrogatories` `general` TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 176 -- can I have discovery or interrogatories` `general` FALSE))

§ `ss 191, 192 -- conduct of the claim`

#ASSERT `ss 191, 192 -- what can follow from how my claim is conducted` `general` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT elem "the Court must take the failure into account in deciding costs (s 191(4))" (`ss 191, 192 -- what can follow from how my claim is conducted` `general` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT elem "an order on your lawyer for your own failure is in the Court's discretion (s 191(5))" (`ss 191, 192 -- what can follow from how my claim is conducted` `general` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT elem "if your lawyer is ordered to bear costs personally for their own failure, they must not recover those costs from you (s 191(6))" (`ss 191, 192 -- what can follow from how my claim is conducted` `general` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT count (`ss 191, 192 -- what can follow from how my claim is conducted` `general` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 8
#ASSERT count (`ss 191, 192 -- what can follow from how my claim is conducted` `general` FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 5
-- s 191A: no s 191 consequences in a Family Law Act proceeding; s 192 still applies.
#ASSERT `ss 191, 192 -- what can follow from how my claim is conducted` `family law` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT count (`ss 191, 192 -- what can follow from how my claim is conducted` `family law` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 5
-- s 191A names only Family Law Act proceedings: child support keeps s 191.
#ASSERT count (`ss 191, 192 -- what can follow from how my claim is conducted` `child support` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 3

§ `ss 156, 161, 168-170 -- dispute resolution`

#ASSERT `ss 161, 169, 170 -- can I be referred` `general` `conciliation (s 161)` FALSE EQUALS `yes, even without my consent`
#ASSERT `ss 161, 169, 170 -- can I be referred` `general` `mediation (s 169)` FALSE EQUALS `yes, even without my consent`
#ASSERT `ss 161, 169, 170 -- can I be referred` `general` `arbitration (s 170)` TRUE EQUALS `yes, but only with my consent (and the other parties')`
#ASSERT `ss 161, 169, 170 -- can I be referred` `general` `arbitration (s 170)` FALSE EQUALS `no: I have not consented, and arbitration needs the consent of the parties (s 170(3))`
#ASSERT `ss 161, 169, 170 -- can I be referred` `family law` `conciliation (s 161)` TRUE EQUALS `not under these sections: the Family Law Act 1975 governs (s 156)`
#ASSERT `ss 161, 169, 170 -- can I be referred` `family law` `arbitration (s 170)` TRUE EQUALS `not under these sections: the Family Law Act 1975 governs (s 156)`
-- Child support: Part 5 applies (conciliation) but not its Division 2 (mediation, arbitration).
#ASSERT `ss 161, 169, 170 -- can I be referred` `child support` `conciliation (s 161)` FALSE EQUALS `yes, even without my consent`
#ASSERT `ss 161, 169, 170 -- can I be referred` `child support` `mediation (s 169)` TRUE EQUALS `not under these sections: child support proceedings are outside Division 2 of Part 5 (s 168)`
#ASSERT `ss 161, 169, 170 -- can I be referred` `child support` `arbitration (s 170)` TRUE EQUALS `not under these sections: child support proceedings are outside Division 2 of Part 5 (s 168)`

#ASSERT `s 169(4) -- can my words at mediation be used in evidence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 169(4) -- can my words at mediation be used in evidence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 169(4) -- can my words at mediation be used in evidence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 172 -- review of an arbitration award, and its costs`

#ASSERT `s 172 -- can I have the arbitration award reviewed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 172 -- can I have the arbitration award reviewed` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not yet registered; no award yet; a private arbitration the Court did not order.
#ASSERT `s 172 -- can I have the arbitration award reviewed` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 172 -- can I have the arbitration award reviewed` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 172 -- can I have the arbitration award reviewed` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- $18,000 claimed, taxed at $12,500: I pay at most $12,500. Taxed above the claim: the claim. No taxation order: no cap.
#ASSERT `s 172(5) -- the most I pay for the arbitration costs` TRUE 18000 12500 EQUALS JUST 12500
#ASSERT `s 172(5) -- the most I pay for the arbitration costs` TRUE 9000 12500 EQUALS JUST 9000
#ASSERT `s 172(5) -- the most I pay for the arbitration costs` TRUE 12500 12500 EQUALS JUST 12500
#ASSERT `s 172(5) -- the most I pay for the arbitration costs` FALSE 18000 12500 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 211 -- interest up to judgment`

-- Arguments: kind, a claim to recover money, applied, interest as of right, consent judgment, interest consented, good cause.
#ASSERT `s 211 -- can I get interest up to judgment` `general` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Court must add interest (or a lump sum instead) to my judgment (s 211(3))`
#ASSERT `s 211 -- can I get interest up to judgment` `general` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not until I apply for an interest order (s 211(2))`
#ASSERT `s 211 -- can I get interest up to judgment` `general` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 211 does not reach it: good cause shown against an order`
#ASSERT `s 211 -- can I get interest up to judgment` `general` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 211(3) does not apply: interest is payable on the debt as of right (s 211(4)(b))`
#ASSERT `s 211 -- can I get interest up to judgment` `general` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no interest under s 211 on a consent judgment unless the parties consent to it (s 211(4)(e))`
#ASSERT `s 211 -- can I get interest up to judgment` `general` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Court must add interest (or a lump sum instead) to my judgment (s 211(3))`
#ASSERT `s 211 -- can I get interest up to judgment` `general` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 211 does not reach it: not a claim for the recovery of money`
#ASSERT `s 211 -- can I get interest up to judgment` `family law` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 211 does not apply: family law or child support (s 211(1))`
#ASSERT `s 211 -- can I get interest up to judgment` `child support` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 211 does not apply: family law or child support (s 211(1))`

-- Judgment of $127,300: $100,000 past loss, $10,000 future loss, $5,000 exemplary, $5,000 unpaid non-interest-bearing
-- liabilities, $7,300 such liabilities paid on 2 July 2025. Cause of action 1 January 2025, judgment 1 January 2026
-- (365 days), rate 5%. Main part: 100,000 x 5% x 365/365 = 5,000. Paid liabilities: 2 July 2025 to 1 January 2026 is
-- 183 days; 7,300 x 5% x 183/365 = 183. Total 5,183.
#ASSERT `s 211 -- the most interest up to judgment` 127300 10000 5000 5000 7300 (`the calendar date` 2 7 2025) (`the calendar date` 1 1 2025) (`the calendar date` 1 1 2026) 5 EQUALS 5183
-- No excluded parts: 100,000 x 5% for 365 days.
#ASSERT `s 211 -- the most interest up to judgment` 100000 0 0 0 0 (`the calendar date` 1 1 2025) (`the calendar date` 1 1 2025) (`the calendar date` 1 1 2026) 5 EQUALS 5000
-- All future loss and exemplary damages: no interest.
#ASSERT `s 211 -- the most interest up to judgment` 50000 30000 20000 0 0 (`the calendar date` 1 1 2025) (`the calendar date` 1 1 2025) (`the calendar date` 1 1 2026) 5 EQUALS 0
-- Across 29 February 2028: 1 March 2027 to 1 March 2028 is 366 days; 36,500 x 10% x 366/365 = 3,660.
#ASSERT `s 211 -- the most interest up to judgment` 36500 0 0 0 0 (`the calendar date` 1 3 2027) (`the calendar date` 1 3 2027) (`the calendar date` 1 3 2028) 10 EQUALS 3660
-- A liability paid after judgment carries no s 211 interest: 36,500 paid 1 April 2028, judgment 1 March 2028.
#ASSERT `s 211 -- the most interest up to judgment` 36500 0 0 0 36500 (`the calendar date` 1 4 2028) (`the calendar date` 1 3 2027) (`the calendar date` 1 3 2028) 10 EQUALS 0
-- Judgment on the day the cause of action arose: no period.
#ASSERT `s 211 -- the most interest up to judgment` 100000 0 0 0 0 (`the calendar date` 1 1 2025) (`the calendar date` 1 1 2025) (`the calendar date` 1 1 2025) 5 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `simple interest on` 73000 `at` 10 `for` 30 EQUALS 600

§ `s 212 -- interest on the judgment debt`

-- $73,000 entered 1 January 2026, paid 31 January 2026 (30 days), Rules rate 10%: 73,000 x 10% x 30/365 = 600.
#ASSERT `s 212 -- interest on my judgment debt` `general` 73000 (`the calendar date` 1 1 2026) (`the calendar date` 31 1 2026) 10 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 600
-- A lower rate of 5% set by the Court: 300.
#ASSERT `s 212 -- interest on my judgment debt` `general` 73000 (`the calendar date` 1 1 2026) (`the calendar date` 31 1 2026) 10 TRUE 5 EQUALS JUST 300
-- A "lower" rate that is not lower: s 212(3)(b) allows only a lower rate, so the Rules rate stands.
#ASSERT `s 212 -- interest on my judgment debt` `general` 73000 (`the calendar date` 1 1 2026) (`the calendar date` 31 1 2026) 10 TRUE 12 EQUALS JUST 600
-- Paid the day judgment is entered.
#ASSERT `s 212 -- interest on my judgment debt` `general` 73000 (`the calendar date` 1 1 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 1 2026) 10 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 212 -- interest on my judgment debt` `family law` 73000 (`the calendar date` 1 1 2026) (`the calendar date` 31 1 2026) 10 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 212 -- interest on my judgment debt` `child support` 73000 (`the calendar date` 1 1 2026) (`the calendar date` 31 1 2026) 10 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 213 -- enforcement`

#ASSERT `s 213 -- how I can enforce my judgment` `family law` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 213 -- how I can enforce my judgment` `general` FALSE EQUALS JUST (LIST "the judgment has effect and may be executed throughout Australia (s 131(3))", "in each State or Territory you have the same enforcement remedies, by execution or otherwise, as a person with a judgment of that State's or Territory's Supreme Court (s 213(2)), subject to the Rules of Court (s 213(3))", "other Acts and the Rules of Court may add further means of enforcement (s 213(4))")
#ASSERT `the answer includes` "but a writ of attachment must not be issued to enforce payment of money under an order in the terms of an arbitration award (s 173(4))" (`s 213 -- how I can enforce my judgment` `general` TRUE)

§ `s 214 -- costs`

#ASSERT `s 214 -- can costs be awarded` `general` `another law` FALSE EQUALS `yes: costs are in the Court's discretion, even if the proceeding is dismissed for want of jurisdiction (s 214(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `s 214 -- can costs be awarded` `general` `another law` TRUE EQUALS `no: another Act says costs must not be awarded in this proceeding (s 214(2))`
#ASSERT `s 214 -- can costs be awarded` `general` `the Fair Work Act 2009` FALSE EQUALS `s 214 does not apply: see Fair Work Act 2009 s 570 (s 214(1)(b)(i))`
#ASSERT `s 214 -- can costs be awarded` `general` `Division 2 of Part IIB of the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986 (an unlawful discrimination claim)` FALSE EQUALS `s 214 does not apply: see Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986 s 46PSA (s 214(1)(b)(ia))`
#ASSERT `s 214 -- can costs be awarded` `general` `section 14, 15 or 16 of the Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013` TRUE EQUALS `s 214 does not apply: see Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 s 18 (s 214(1)(b)(ii))`
#ASSERT `s 214 -- can costs be awarded` `child support` `another law` FALSE EQUALS `s 214 does not apply: family law or child support (see Family Law Act 1975 s 114UB) (s 214(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `s 214 -- can costs be awarded` `family law` `the Fair Work Act 2009` FALSE EQUALS `s 214 does not apply: family law or child support (see Family Law Act 1975 s 114UB) (s 214(1)(a))`

§ `s 215 -- security for costs`

-- Ordered 1 March 2026 to give security by 29 March 2026 (28 days).
#ASSERT `s 215 -- where my security for costs stands` `general` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 29 3 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 29 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `given in time: s 215(5) is not engaged`
#ASSERT `s 215 -- where my security for costs stands` `general` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 29 3 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 30 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `not given in time: the Court may dismiss my proceeding or stay it until security is given (s 215(5))`
#ASSERT `s 215 -- where my security for costs stands` `general` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 29 3 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `given in time: s 215(5) is not engaged`
#ASSERT `s 215 -- where my security for costs stands` `general` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 29 3 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 1 2000) (`the calendar date` 29 3 2026) EQUALS `not yet due: give it by the last day`
#ASSERT `s 215 -- where my security for costs stands` `general` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 29 3 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 1 2000) (`the calendar date` 30 3 2026) EQUALS `not given in time: the Court may dismiss my proceeding or stay it until security is given (s 215(5))`
-- Across 29 February 2028: ordered 15 February 2028, last day 29 February 2028; given 29 February in time, 1 March late.
#ASSERT `s 215 -- where my security for costs stands` `general` (`the calendar date` 15 2 2028) (`the calendar date` 29 2 2028) TRUE (`the calendar date` 29 2 2028) (`the calendar date` 1 3 2028) EQUALS `given in time: s 215(5) is not engaged`
#ASSERT `s 215 -- where my security for costs stands` `general` (`the calendar date` 15 2 2028) (`the calendar date` 29 2 2028) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2028) (`the calendar date` 1 3 2028) EQUALS `not given in time: the Court may dismiss my proceeding or stay it until security is given (s 215(5))`
#ASSERT `s 215 -- where my security for costs stands` `family law` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 29 3 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 1 2000) (`the calendar date` 30 3 2026) EQUALS `s 215 does not apply: family law or child support (s 215(1))`
-- The regulative rule directly: day 28 of 28 in time, day 29 late, day 0 in time.
#ASSERT `s 215 -- security given on this day is in time` 28 28
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 215 -- security given on this day is in time` 28 29))
#ASSERT `s 215 -- security given on this day is in time` 28 0

§ `s 256 -- review of a Registrar's decision`

-- Decided 10 February 2026; the Rules allow 14 days (an input here): last day 24 February 2026.
#ASSERT `s 256 -- can I have the delegate's decision reviewed` (`the calendar date` 10 2 2026) 14 TRUE (`the calendar date` 24 2 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `yes: I applied (or can apply) in time (s 256(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `s 256 -- can I have the delegate's decision reviewed` (`the calendar date` 10 2 2026) 14 TRUE (`the calendar date` 25 2 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `only if further time is allowed under the Rules (s 256(1)(b)); the Court may also review on its own initiative (s 256(2))`
#ASSERT `s 256 -- can I have the delegate's decision reviewed` (`the calendar date` 10 2 2026) 14 TRUE (`the calendar date` 25 2 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS `yes: within the further time allowed (s 256(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `s 256 -- can I have the delegate's decision reviewed` (`the calendar date` 10 2 2026) 14 FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 1 2000) (`the calendar date` 24 2 2026) FALSE EQUALS `yes: I applied (or can apply) in time (s 256(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `s 256 -- can I have the delegate's decision reviewed` (`the calendar date` 10 2 2026) 14 FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 1 2000) (`the calendar date` 25 2 2026) FALSE EQUALS `only if further time is allowed under the Rules (s 256(1)(b)); the Court may also review on its own initiative (s 256(2))`
-- Across 29 February 2028: decided 15 February 2028, 14 days: 29 February in time, 1 March not.
#ASSERT `s 256 -- can I have the delegate's decision reviewed` (`the calendar date` 15 2 2028) 14 TRUE (`the calendar date` 29 2 2028) (`the calendar date` 1 3 2028) FALSE EQUALS `yes: I applied (or can apply) in time (s 256(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `s 256 -- can I have the delegate's decision reviewed` (`the calendar date` 15 2 2028) 14 TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2028) (`the calendar date` 1 3 2028) FALSE EQUALS `only if further time is allowed under the Rules (s 256(1)(b)); the Court may also review on its own initiative (s 256(2))`
#ASSERT `s 256 -- an application on this day is in time` 14 14
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 256 -- an application on this day is in time` 14 15))

§ `ss 26, 28, 149, 153 -- appeals from Division 2`

`final` MEANS `a judgment deciding the case, or another order`
`disqualify` MEANS `a decision rejecting my application that the Judge disqualify themself`

#ASSERT `ss 26, 28 -- can I appeal from Division 2` `family law` `final` FALSE EQUALS `yes, to Division 1 (s 26(1)(c) or (h)); no leave needed`
#ASSERT `ss 26, 28 -- can I appeal from Division 2` `family law` `final` TRUE EQUALS `yes, to Division 1, but only with the leave of Division 1 (s 28(1))`
#ASSERT `ss 26, 28 -- can I appeal from Division 2` `child support` `final` FALSE EQUALS `yes, to Division 1, but only with the leave of Division 1 (s 28(1))`
#ASSERT `ss 26, 28 -- can I appeal from Division 2` `child support` `disqualify` FALSE EQUALS `yes, to Division 1, but only with the leave of Division 1 (s 28(1))`
#ASSERT `ss 26, 28 -- can I appeal from Division 2` `family law` `disqualify` FALSE EQUALS `yes, to Division 1 (s 26(1)(c) or (h)); no leave needed`
-- s 28(1)(c) adds leave for a disqualification decision in child support jurisdiction; it takes nothing from (b): a disqualification decision that is itself prescribed needs leave (s 7: a judgment includes a decision).
#ASSERT `ss 26, 28 -- can I appeal from Division 2` `family law` `disqualify` TRUE EQUALS `yes, to Division 1, but only with the leave of Division 1 (s 28(1))`
#ASSERT `ss 26, 28 -- can I appeal from Division 2` `family law` `a decision to join or remove a party` FALSE EQUALS `no appeal from this kind of decision (s 26(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `ss 26, 28 -- can I appeal from Division 2` `child support` `a decision to adjourn or expedite a hearing` FALSE EQUALS `no appeal from this kind of decision (s 26(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `ss 26, 28 -- can I appeal from Division 2` `family law` `a decision to vacate a hearing date` TRUE EQUALS `no appeal from this kind of decision (s 26(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `ss 26, 28 -- can I appeal from Division 2` `family law` `a decision about transferring the proceeding to Division 1 or the Federal Court` FALSE EQUALS `no appeal from a transfer decision (s 149(4), s 153(6))`
#ASSERT `ss 26, 28 -- can I appeal from Division 2` `general` `a decision about transferring the proceeding to Division 1 or the Federal Court` FALSE EQUALS `no appeal from a transfer decision (s 149(4), s 153(6))`
#ASSERT `ss 26, 28 -- can I appeal from Division 2` `general` `final` FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not give the appeal; see the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976`
#ASSERT `ss 26, 28 -- can I appeal from Division 2` `general` `a decision to join or remove a party` FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not give the appeal; see the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976`

§ `ss 55, 155 -- the High Court`

#ASSERT `ss 55, 155 -- can I appeal to the High Court` `a judgment of Division 2` EQUALS `not directly (s 55(1) or s 155(1)), save by special leave if the bar would be inconsistent with Constitution s 73 (s 55(6), s 155(2))`
#ASSERT `ss 55, 155 -- can I appeal to the High Court` `a judgment of Division 1 in its original jurisdiction` EQUALS `not directly (s 55(1) or s 155(1)), save by special leave if the bar would be inconsistent with Constitution s 73 (s 55(6), s 155(2))`
#ASSERT `ss 55, 155 -- can I appeal to the High Court` `a judgment of a single Judge of Division 1 on appeal from a State or Territory court of summary jurisdiction` EQUALS `not directly (s 55(1) or s 155(1)), save by special leave if the bar would be inconsistent with Constitution s 73 (s 55(6), s 155(2))`
#ASSERT `ss 55, 155 -- can I appeal to the High Court` `a judgment of Division 1 on another appeal, deciding the appeal` EQUALS `only by special leave of the High Court (s 55(2))`
#ASSERT `ss 55, 155 -- can I appeal to the High Court` `a procedural decision of Division 1 on an appeal (extension of time, leave to amend grounds, stay, security for costs, joining or removing a party, leave to defend, reinstatement, adjourning, expediting or vacating a hearing)` EQUALS `no appeal to the High Court (s 55(3))`

§ `ss 228-236 -- suppression and non-publication orders`

`identity` MEANS `information that could identify, or is about, a party or witness, or someone related to or associated with them`

#ASSERT `ss 230, 231 -- can the information be suppressed` `general` `identity` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Court may make the order, specifying the ground and limited to what its purpose needs (ss 230, 231, 232(5), 234)`
#ASSERT `ss 230, 231 -- can the information be suppressed` `general` `information obtained by discovery` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Court may make the order, specifying the ground and limited to what its purpose needs (ss 230, 231, 232(5), 234)`
#ASSERT `ss 230, 231 -- can the information be suppressed` `general` `information lodged with or filed in the Court` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Court may make the order, specifying the ground and limited to what its purpose needs (ss 230, 231, 232(5), 234)`
-- Ground (d) needs both a sexual offence case and undue distress.
#ASSERT `ss 230, 231 -- can the information be suppressed` `general` `evidence, or information about evidence` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Court may make the order, specifying the ground and limited to what its purpose needs (ss 230, 231, 232(5), 234)`
#ASSERT `ss 230, 231 -- can the information be suppressed` `general` `identity` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: no ground the Act permits is made out (ss 230(1), 231(1))`
#ASSERT `ss 230, 231 -- can the information be suppressed` `general` `identity` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: no ground the Act permits is made out (ss 230(1), 231(1))`
-- Embarrassment alone, in a civil claim: no ground.
#ASSERT `ss 230, 231 -- can the information be suppressed` `general` `identity` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: no ground the Act permits is made out (ss 230(1), 231(1))`
#ASSERT `ss 230, 231 -- can the information be suppressed` `general` `other information` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 230 does not reach this information`
#ASSERT `ss 230, 231 -- can the information be suppressed` `family law` `identity` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Part 7 does not apply: Family Law Act 1975 Part XIA governs (s 228)`
-- Child support is not a Family Law Act proceeding: Part 7 applies.
#ASSERT `ss 230, 231 -- can the information be suppressed` `child support` `identity` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Court may make the order, specifying the ground and limited to what its purpose needs (ss 230, 231, 232(5), 234)`

